#: ../../tools/kegg_conv_link_tools.rst:65 3b5b6294597743cd936c09236bace03b
msgid "**Name**: ``KEGG_link_entries``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/kegg_conv_link_tools.rst:67 37f57d67466945b5abadea06ac09a2ec
msgid ""
"**Description**: Find cross-references between KEGG databases using the "
"KEGG /link API. Given a KEGG entry (gene, pathway, disease, drug, "
"compound), find all linked entries in another KEGG database. Examples: "
"find all diseases for gene hsa:7157 (TP53), all genes in a pathway, or "
"all pathways for a compound. Complements KEGG\\_get\\_gene\\_pathways "
"with more flexible cross-database queries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/kegg_conv_link_tools.rst:71 fa75f172c4cf4dc8a7c667ca034e50b0
msgid ""
"``source`` (string) (required) KEGG entry ID to query. Examples: "
"'hsa:7157' (gene), 'hsa05200' (pathway), 'H00004' (disease), 'D00279' "
"(drug), 'C00002' (compound)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/kegg_conv_link_tools.rst:74 bd68e79416f945b29997f365a87158e4
msgid ""
"``target`` (string) (required) Target KEGG database to search for links. "
"Options: 'pathway', 'disease', 'drug', 'compound', 'ko' (orthology), "
"'enzyme', 'reaction', 'module'. Can also use organism prefix for genes "
"(e.g., 'hsa')."
msgstr ""

